// Title: LiveKD Kernel Memory Dump File Created
// Sigma ID: 814ddeca-3d31-4265-8e07-8cc54fb44903
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth
// Description: Detects the creation of a file that has the same name as the default LiveKD kernel memory dump.
// False positives:
//   - In rare occasions administrators might leverage LiveKD to perform live kernel debugging. This should not be allowed on production systems. Investigate and apply additional filters where necessary.
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_sysinternals_livekd_default_dump_name.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\livekd.dmp"
